PROJECT
 ↓
MODEL VERSION 1
 ↓
REVISION 1
The project shall receive a UUID.

19. PROJECT MUTATION
Every project mutation must specify the expected current revision.
Example:
expected_revision = 14
The service compares:
requested revision
against:
current project revision
If they differ, the command shall not silently modify the newer state.
This establishes optimistic concurrency control.

20. MODEL VERSION CREATION
A successful model mutation creates a new model version.
Conceptually:
MODEL VERSION 14
       ↓
COMMAND
       ↓
MODEL VERSION 15
The previous model version remains immutable.

21. REVISION CREATION
A completed model mutation creates a revision record.
Conceptually:
Revision 14
     ↓
Move Element
     ↓
Revision 15
The revision contains:
parent_revision_id
model_version_id
created_by
reason
status
validation_summary
code_manifest_id

22. CHANGE RECORD
Every mutation shall generate a change record.
Example:
object_id
operation = MOVE_ELEMENT
before_state = {...}
after_state = {...}
reason = "User requested wall relocation"
source = "ARIA"
The change record becomes part of historical reconstruction.

23. EVENT RECORDING
