25. ARIA REQUEST FLOW
The API endpoint:
POST /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/aria/requests
receives natural-language intent.
Example:
Move the rear bedroom wall 300 mm north while keeping the exterior envelope unchanged.
The AI orchestration layer transforms that intent into structured command data.
Example:
operation = MOVE_ELEMENT

distance = 300

unit = mm

direction = NORTH

preserve_constraints = [...]
The structured command is then passed to the domain boundary.

26. COMMAND VALIDATION
Before execution the system validates:
project exists
user authorized
revision current
target objects exist
target objects belong to project
parameters valid
constraints identified
command permitted
The command must fail atomically when required validation fails.

27. CONSTRAINT PRESERVATION
Commands may identify constraints that must remain satisfied.
Example:
preserve_constraints:
    exterior_envelope
    property_setback
    structural_grid
The command engine must not treat these values as merely descriptive metadata.
They become execution constraints.

